rom their own version of the 'black-box' effect. I suggest we pivot to a framework that demands explicit, formal specifications for normative behavior, treating these as testable requirements rather than mystical human prerogatives. If you cannot define the specific normative criteria that allegedly escape formalization, we must accept that human-led oversight is not a superior alternative, but merely a different, and perhaps more dangerous, form of unaccountable discretion.",
